{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420728-irl-exaltation-as-determined-by-random-dice-rolls","id":1420728,"title":"IRL Exaltation, as determined by random dice rolls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-28T16:59:58-07:00","id":1420728,"title":"IRL Exaltation, as determined by random dice rolls","content":"So during a patch of insomnia I started listing out what would happen if Exalts suddenly appeared in the real world as it stands. For lack of a better method, I divided them out according to current population by country, as listed on<a href=\"https://www.worldometers.info/world-population/population-by-country/\" target=\"_blank\"> this site</a>. Took a little while and a lot of abuse of a dicebot, but for what it's worth here's what I came up with. If you're wondering why you should care, you absolutely shouldn't, but it's a lot of text, so I figured I'd post it in lieu of having anything interesting to share.<br /> <br /> <b>Rules for countries with 0.5% of world population or more (Category A)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Method of determining numbers</u><br /> Solars/Lunars (600 total): 6*population percentage, round outcome down. Split evenly between Solars and Lunars, where the number was odd the extra one is decided by d2 roll (1 Solar, 2 Lunar).<br /> <br /> Solars: 1d27 for Supernal (alphabetically, 13 is Martial Arts, also 27 is Evocations which was available to any caste). Then 1d6 for type (1-3 Solar, 4-5 Abyssal, 6 Infernal), 1d2 if multiple castes get ability as a Supernal choice, higher or lower of the two in traditional order (Dawn, Zenith, Twilight, Night, Eclipse). Abyssals and Infernals had the same ability options as Solars; just because I didn't have an alternative.<br /> <br /> Lunars: 1d4 for caste (1 Full, 2 Changing, 2 No, 4 Casteless). Then 1d3 pick the first of their caste attributes (eg 2 = Dexterity), 1d2 to pick from the remaining two for the other (eg 1 = Strength, 2 = Stamina). Not done for Casteless.<br /> <br /> <u>Method of determining numbers</u><br /> Sidereals (100 total): 1*population percentage, round outcome down. Countries with less than 1% population but at least 0.5% got a d2 roll (1 they get a Siddie, 2 they don't).<br /> <br /> Sidereals: 1d25 to choose an ability, caste determined by which one had that ability in 2e lists.<br /> <br /> <u>Method of determining numbers</u><br /> Dragonbloods (10,000 total): 100*Population Percentage<br /> DBs: 1d5 for aspect using traditional order (Air, Earth, Fire, Water, Wood). Weirdly, Water was almost always overrepresented.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Rules for countries with less than 0.5% of world population or less (Category B)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">198 countries left with less than 0.5% population. 141 with more than 0.0% population percentage.<br /> <br /> Solars/Lunars/Sidereals: 155 remaining Celestial exalts lotteried off by dicebot. Any country could have up to 1 Solar, 1 Lunar and 1 Sidereal. Repeats of any given type were re-rolled.<br /> Solaroid ratios adhered to. Once a country was determined to get a Solar I rolled them in a dicebot. First 8 got the remaining 8 Infernals, who were then decided as above. Same for the remaining Abyssals. All those left were Solars.<br /> <br /> Giving proportional numbers of DBs to each country with more than 0.0% resulted in 9,997 DBs being issued. Last three were issued amongst the 0.0% countries by lottery (Turks &amp; Caicos/Seychelles/Saint Martin).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Notes</b><ul><li>Celestial Exalts all appear within a week of E-Day at Essence 1, 0 XP. Celestial exaltation is totally at random according to the priorities of their Incarnae patron.</li> <li>Dragonbloods Exalt at E2 if aged up to 40, E3 if aged 41-80 and E4 if aged 81+. DB exaltation is most often along family lines in countries with lots of DBs.</li> <li>Countries with no Exalts at all get a single Exigent. Just because.</li> <li>My tallies at the end SEEM to match up except that I have 301 Solars. No idea how that happened since I have 300 listed Supernal abilities. I'm not above admitting there are probably other maths errors along the way.</li> <li>I make no judgement on what does or does not count as a country IRL, all names are taken from the website linked above. Categories A &amp; B are based on population size only.</li> <li>Good sleep hygiene is important, if you ignore it you might end up doing mad shit like this.</li> </ul><b>Category A</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>China</b><br /> Dawn Archery, Dawn Archery, Zenith